WEBVTT

00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:10.744
Previously on Supernatural.

00:00:13.543 --> 00:00:17.101
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:18.446 --> 00:00:20.024
Mary! No!

00:00:21.784 --> 00:00:22.923
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:24.048 --> 00:00:25.599
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:27.565 --> 00:00:28.964
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.146
I can't do this alone.

00:00:36.785 --> 00:00:38.089
We got work to do.

00:00:38.459 --> 00:00:39.722
This is dad's single

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:41.039
Most valuable possession.

00:00:41.066 --> 00:00:43.371
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:43.413 --> 00:00:45.380
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:45.421 --> 00:00:46.724
You know, saving people,

00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:47.836
Hunting things...

00:00:47.877 --> 00:00:48.755
Family business.

00:00:48.817 --> 00:00:49.283
No.

00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:50.696
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:52.206
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.108
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:57.310
Yeah, I know.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:13.740
Morning, daddy.

00:01:13.802 --> 00:01:15.179
Morning, sweetheart.

00:01:17.406 --> 00:01:19.674
All these workouts, Soph, I don't know.

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:21.599
Guys don't like buff girls.

00:01:21.693 --> 00:01:24.561
Yeah, well, girls don't like
guys who still live at home.

00:01:31.465 --> 00:01:32.873
Be careful.

00:01:32.936 --> 00:01:34.031
I will.

00:03:10.337 --> 00:03:11.902
Can I get you anything else?

00:03:15.109 --> 00:03:16.674
Just the check, please.

00:03:16.772 --> 00:03:17.679
Okay.

00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:25.707
You know, Sam, we are allowed
to have fun once in a while.

00:03:28.538 --> 00:03:29.634
That's fun.

00:03:33.972 --> 00:03:35.990
Here, take a look at
this. I think I got one.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.930
Lake Manitoc, Wisconsin.

00:03:38.102 --> 00:03:39.729
Last week, Sophie Carlton,

00:03:39.828 --> 00:03:42.049
18, walks into the lake,

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.317
Doesn't walk out.

00:03:43.364 --> 00:03:45.038
Authorities dragged the water.

00:03:45.116 --> 00:03:46.008
Nothing.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.048
Sophie Carlton is the third
Lake Manitoc drowning this year.

00:03:49.173 --> 00:03:50.941
None of the other
bodies were found, either

00:03:51.082 --> 00:03:52.224
They had a funeral two days ago.

00:03:52.286 --> 00:03:52.897
A funeral?

00:03:52.943 --> 00:03:54.977
Yes, they buried an empty coffin.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:58.114
For closure or whatever.

00:03:58.349 --> 00:03:59.428
Closure?

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.508
What closure?

00:04:01.712 --> 00:04:03.480
People don't just disappear, Dean.

00:04:03.714 --> 00:04:05.670
Other people just stop looking for them.

00:04:07.458 --> 00:04:08.553
Something you want to say to me?

00:04:08.589 --> 00:04:11.327
The trail for dad. It's getting colder.

00:04:11.452 --> 00:04:12.031
Every day.

00:04:12.062 --> 00:04:14.080
What are we supposed
to do? I don't know.

00:04:14.299 --> 00:04:15.128
Something.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:16.411
Anything. No one.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.840
I'm sick of this attitude.

00:04:18.168 --> 00:04:19.749
You don't think I want to
find dad as much as you do?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.562
Yeah, I know you do it.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.269
I'm the one that's been with him every
single day for the past two years.

00:04:23.378 --> 00:04:25.569
While you've been off to
college going to pep rallies.

00:04:25.709 --> 00:04:26.898
We will find dad,

00:04:26.961 --> 00:04:29.167
But until then, we're
gonna kill everything bad,

00:04:29.307 --> 00:04:30.841
Between here and there.

00:04:31.654 --> 00:04:32.703
Okay?

00:04:39.361 --> 00:04:41.332
All right, Lake Manitoc.

00:04:42.036 --> 00:04:42.411
Hey.

00:04:42.521 --> 00:04:42.959
Huh?

00:04:43.006 --> 00:04:43.804
How far?

00:05:05.103 --> 00:05:05.963
Will Carlton?

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.027
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:07.183 --> 00:05:08.247
I'm agent Ford.

00:05:08.428 --> 00:05:09.773
This is agent Hamill.

00:05:10.258 --> 00:05:12.042
We're with the U.S. Wildlife service.

00:05:19.344 --> 00:05:21.221
She was about 100 yards out.

00:05:22.848 --> 00:05:23.943
That's where she got dragged down.

00:05:24.006 --> 00:05:25.351
And you're sure she didn't just drown?

00:05:25.383 --> 00:05:25.821
Yeah.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.573
She was a varsity swimmer.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.450
She practically grew up in that lake.

00:05:30.576 --> 00:05:32.751
She's as safe out there
as in her own bathtub.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.597
So no splashing,

00:05:34.691 --> 00:05:35.802
No signs of distress?

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:37.006
No, that's what I'm telling you.

00:05:37.183 --> 00:05:39.326
Did you see any shadows in the water,

00:05:40.171 --> 00:05:41.016
Maybe,

00:05:41.219 --> 00:05:43.659
Some dark shape breach the surface?

00:05:43.706 --> 00:05:45.724
No, again, she was really far out there.

00:05:45.818 --> 00:05:47.570
You ever see any strange
tracks by the shoreline?

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:48.509
No, never.

00:05:48.618 --> 00:05:49.432
Why?

00:05:49.557 --> 00:05:50.903
What do you think's out there?

00:05:51.357 --> 00:05:53.641
We'll let you know as soon as we do.

00:05:55.878 --> 00:05:57.380
What about your father?

00:05:57.615 --> 00:05:59.070
Can we talk to him?

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:01.782
Look.

00:06:01.891 --> 00:06:03.377
If you don't mind, I mean,

00:06:03.581 --> 00:06:06.100
He didn't see anything, and
he's kind of been through a lot.

00:06:06.991 --> 00:06:08.243
We understand.

00:06:14.598 --> 00:06:15.542
Now, I'm sorry, but,

00:06:15.568 --> 00:06:19.767
Why does the wildlife service
care about an accidental drowning?

00:06:19.902 --> 00:06:21.247
You sure it's accidental?

00:06:21.503 --> 00:06:23.489
Will Carlton saw
something grab his sister.

00:06:24.053 --> 00:06:25.195
Like what?

00:06:25.633 --> 00:06:26.665
Here, sit, please.

00:06:26.712 --> 00:06:29.748
There are no indigenous
carnivores in that lake.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.642
There's nothing even big
enough to pull down a person,

00:06:32.728 --> 00:06:34.574
Unless it was the Loch Ness monster.

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:36.882
Yeah, right.

00:06:37.007 --> 00:06:41.075
Will Carlton was traumatized, and
sometimes the mind plays tricks.

00:06:41.502 --> 00:06:42.362
Still,

00:06:42.894 --> 00:06:46.461
We dragged that entire lake.
We even ran a sonar sweep,

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:49.282
Just to be sure, and there
was nothing down there.

00:06:49.361 --> 00:06:51.410
That's weird, though.

00:06:51.817 --> 00:06:53.444
That's the third missing body this year.

00:06:53.527 --> 00:06:54.622
I know.

00:06:55.279 --> 00:06:57.063
These are people from my town.

00:06:57.251 --> 00:06:58.721
These are people I care about.

00:06:58.815 --> 00:06:59.644
I know.

00:07:01.026 --> 00:07:02.074
Anyway . . .

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:05.031
All this.

00:07:06.361 --> 00:07:08.239
It won't be a problem much longer.

00:07:08.817 --> 00:07:09.866
What do you mean?

00:07:10.654 --> 00:07:12.188
Well, the dam, of course.

00:07:13.502 --> 00:07:14.691
Of course.

00:07:14.957 --> 00:07:15.864
The dam.

00:07:16.177 --> 00:07:17.210
It's, uh...

00:07:18.649 --> 00:07:19.494
It sprung a leak.

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:20.699
It's falling apart,

00:07:21.309 --> 00:07:24.067
And the feds won't give
us the grant to repair it,

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.820
So they've opened the spillway.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:28.229
In another six months,

00:07:28.839 --> 00:07:30.263
There won't be much of a lake.

00:07:30.513 --> 00:07:32.082
There won't be much of a town, either,

00:07:32.223 --> 00:07:33.287
But as federal wildlife,

00:07:33.412 --> 00:07:34.805
You already knew that.

00:07:35.509 --> 00:07:36.338
Exactly.

00:07:36.995 --> 00:07:38.935
Sorry, am I interrupting?

00:07:39.472 --> 00:07:40.692
I think come back later.

00:07:40.833 --> 00:07:42.835
Gentlemen, this is my daughter.

00:07:43.258 --> 00:07:44.447
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:45.714
I'm Dean.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.482
Andrea Bar. Hi.

00:07:47.686 --> 00:07:48.108
Hi.

00:07:48.332 --> 00:07:49.849
They're from the wildlife service,

00:07:50.459 --> 00:07:51.711
About the lake.

00:07:55.878 --> 00:07:57.208
Oh, hey, there.

00:07:57.494 --> 00:07:58.448
What's your name?

00:08:04.769 --> 00:08:06.099
His name is Lucas.

00:08:08.974 --> 00:08:09.850
Is he okay?

00:08:09.928 --> 00:08:11.555
My grandson's been through a lot.

00:08:12.478 --> 00:08:13.793
We all have.

00:08:14.669 --> 00:08:15.482
Well,

00:08:16.254 --> 00:08:17.818
If there's anything
else I can do for you,

00:08:17.835 --> 00:08:18.899
Please, let me know.

00:08:19.023 --> 00:08:19.774
Thanks.

00:08:20.655 --> 00:08:22.360
You know, now that you mentioned it,

00:08:22.454 --> 00:08:25.693
Could you point us in the direction
of a reasonably priced motel?

00:08:25.885 --> 00:08:28.592
Lake front motel, go around
the corner, it's two blocks up.

00:08:28.655 --> 00:08:29.374
Two.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.001
Would you mind showing us?

00:08:32.394 --> 00:08:34.068
You want me to walk you two blocks?

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:35.429
Not if it's any trouble.

00:08:36.038 --> 00:08:37.900
I'm headed that way anyway.

00:08:39.042 --> 00:08:41.092
I'll be back to pick up lucas at 3:00.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.922
We'll go to the park, okay, sweetie?

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:47.981
Thanks again.

00:08:49.045 --> 00:08:50.265
So, cute kid.

00:08:50.625 --> 00:08:51.204
Thanks.

00:08:53.353 --> 00:08:54.824
Kids are the best, huh?

00:08:58.630 --> 00:08:59.960
There it is.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.072
Like I said, two blocks.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:02.917
Thanks.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.171
Must be hard with your
sense of direction,

00:09:06.547 --> 00:09:09.441
Never being able to find your
way to a decent pickup line.

00:09:10.979 --> 00:09:12.215
Enjoy your stay.

00:09:14.077 --> 00:09:15.204
"Kids are the best"?

00:09:15.803 --> 00:09:17.649
You don't even like kids. I love kids.

00:09:17.712 --> 00:09:19.949
Name three children that you even know.

00:09:26.676 --> 00:09:27.740
I'm thinking.

00:09:28.147 --> 00:09:30.650
So there's the three
drowning victims this year.

00:09:30.681 --> 00:09:31.620
And before that?

00:09:31.761 --> 00:09:34.530
Yeah, six more,

00:09:34.561 --> 00:09:36.141
Spread outover the past 35 years.

00:09:36.282 --> 00:09:38.081
Those bodies were
never recovered, either.

00:09:38.691 --> 00:09:40.178
If there is something out there,

00:09:40.328 --> 00:09:41.283
It's picking up its pace.

00:09:41.345 --> 00:09:42.863
So we got a lake monster on a binge?

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.601
This whole lake monster
theory, it just bugs me.

00:09:45.867 --> 00:09:46.712
Why?

00:09:47.249 --> 00:09:49.001
Loch Ness, lake Champlain

00:09:49.032 --> 00:09:51.598
There are literally hundreds
of eyewitness accounts,

00:09:51.645 --> 00:09:53.507
But here, almost nothing.

00:09:53.835 --> 00:09:55.115
Whatever it is out there,

00:09:55.416 --> 00:09:56.777
Noone's living to talk about it.

00:09:57.028 --> 00:09:58.295
Wait, Bar,

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.428
Christopher Bar, where have
I heard that name before?

00:10:00.459 --> 00:10:03.072
Christopher Bar, the victim in may.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.639
Christopher Bar was Andrea's husband,

00:10:06.934 --> 00:10:08.373
Lucas' father.

00:10:08.831 --> 00:10:09.708
Apparently,

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:11.773
He took Lucas out swimming.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:15.246
Lucas was on a floating wooden
platform when Chris drowned,

00:10:15.543 --> 00:10:16.685
Two hours,

00:10:17.124 --> 00:10:18.970
Before the kid got rescued.

00:10:22.677 --> 00:10:24.711
Maybe we have an eyewitness after all.

00:10:25.196 --> 00:10:27.011
No wonder that kid was so freaked out.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:30.958
Watching one of your parents die
isn't something you just get over.

00:10:33.133 --> 00:10:34.385
Can we join you?

00:10:38.377 --> 00:10:39.801
I'm here with my son.

00:10:43.196 --> 00:10:44.432
Mind if I say hi?

00:10:46.786 --> 00:10:50.212
Tell your friend this whole "jerry
maguire" thing's not gonna work on me.

00:10:51.026 --> 00:10:52.700
I don't think that's what this is about.

00:10:55.991 --> 00:10:57.133
How's it going?

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.826
Oh, I used to love these things.

00:11:13.495 --> 00:11:15.451
So crayons is more your thing?

00:11:15.983 --> 00:11:17.970
That's cool. Chicks dig artists.

00:11:20.425 --> 00:11:21.786
Hey, these are pretty good.

00:11:23.366 --> 00:11:25.431
You mind if I sit and
draw with you for a while?

00:11:25.874 --> 00:11:27.454
I'm not so bad myself.

00:11:36.964 --> 00:11:38.826
You know, I'm thinking you can hear me.

00:11:39.373 --> 00:11:40.797
You just don't want to talk.

00:11:41.345 --> 00:11:43.535
I don't know exactly
what happened to your dad,

00:11:44.637 --> 00:11:46.501
But I know it was something real bad.

00:11:50.005 --> 00:11:51.585
I think I know how you feel.

00:11:54.041 --> 00:11:56.325
When I was your age, I saw something.

00:12:03.208 --> 00:12:04.397
Anyway . . .

00:12:06.404 --> 00:12:09.221
Maybe you don't think
anyone will listen to you.

00:12:09.961 --> 00:12:10.947
Or, uh...

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.963
Or believe you.

00:12:14.573 --> 00:12:16.341
I want you to know that I will.

00:12:17.749 --> 00:12:19.266
You don't even have to

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.331
Say anything. You
could draw me a picture,

00:12:21.394 --> 00:12:22.740
About what you saw that day,

00:12:23.038 --> 00:12:24.274
With your dad,

00:12:25.572 --> 00:12:26.433
On the lake.

00:12:30.517 --> 00:12:31.425
Okay,

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:32.535
No problem.

00:12:33.005 --> 00:12:34.022
This is for you.

00:12:35.148 --> 00:12:36.462
This is my family.

00:12:37.761 --> 00:12:38.997
That's my dad.

00:12:39.362 --> 00:12:40.206
That's...

00:12:41.912 --> 00:12:42.944
That's my mom.

00:12:43.715 --> 00:12:45.311
That's my geek brother,

00:12:46.203 --> 00:12:47.392
And that's me.

00:12:51.288 --> 00:12:52.977
All right, so I'm a sucky artist.

00:12:53.404 --> 00:12:54.765
I'll see you around, Lucas.

00:13:07.971 --> 00:13:10.912
Lucas hasn't said a
word, not even to me,

00:13:11.527 --> 00:13:12.623
Not since

00:13:13.577 --> 00:13:15.157
His dad's accident.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:16.972
Yeah, we heard.

00:13:17.254 --> 00:13:18.177
Sorry.

00:13:19.303 --> 00:13:21.102
What are the doctors saying?

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.879
That it's a kind of
post-Traumatic stress.

00:13:23.973 --> 00:13:25.194
That can't be easy

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:26.054
For either of you.

00:13:26.117 --> 00:13:27.619
We moved in with my dad.

00:13:28.589 --> 00:13:30.247
He helps out a lot.

00:13:32.242 --> 00:13:33.384
It's just...

00:13:34.964 --> 00:13:38.312
When I think about what Lucas
went through, what he saw...

00:13:40.659 --> 00:13:41.926
Kids are strong.

00:13:42.486 --> 00:13:44.504
You'd be surprised
what they can deal with.

00:13:45.302 --> 00:13:46.366
You know,

00:13:46.883 --> 00:13:48.494
He used to have such life.

00:13:48.776 --> 00:13:51.169
He was hard to keep up
with, to tell you the truth.

00:13:52.369 --> 00:13:53.761
Now he just sits there,

00:13:53.871 --> 00:13:56.483
Drawing those pictures,
playing with those army men.

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.022
I just wish.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:13:59.805
Hey, sweetie.

00:14:05.318 --> 00:14:06.100
Thanks.

00:14:07.132 --> 00:14:08.259
Thanks, Lucas.

00:14:26.375 --> 00:14:27.627
Hey, dad.

00:14:29.019 --> 00:14:30.834
You should probably eat something.

00:14:32.982 --> 00:14:34.547
I'm gonna make some dinner, okay?

00:16:29.125 --> 00:16:30.189
So,

00:16:30.299 --> 00:16:32.317
I think it's safe to say
we can rule out Nessie.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:33.146
What do you mean?

00:16:33.229 --> 00:16:36.358
I just drove past the Carlton
house. There was an ambulance there.

00:16:36.561 --> 00:16:37.907
Will Carlton is dead.

00:16:38.141 --> 00:16:38.720
He drowned?

00:16:38.767 --> 00:16:40.379
Yep, in the sink.

00:16:41.098 --> 00:16:42.240
What the hell?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.858
So this isn't a creature. We're
dealing with something else.

00:16:44.905 --> 00:16:45.687
Yeah, but what?

00:16:45.734 --> 00:16:46.344
I don't know.

00:16:46.469 --> 00:16:47.611
A water wraith maybe?

00:16:47.846 --> 00:16:48.925
Some kind of demon?

00:16:49.137 --> 00:16:50.811
I mean, something that controls water

00:16:53.242 --> 00:16:54.791
water that comes from the Same source.

00:16:54.854 --> 00:16:55.667
The lake Yeah

00:16:55.699 --> 00:16:57.607
Which would explain why
it's upping the body count.

00:16:57.983 --> 00:17:00.877
The lake is draining. It'll be dry in
a few months. Whatever this thing is,

00:17:00.949 --> 00:17:02.388
Whatever it wants,

00:17:02.717 --> 00:17:03.577
It's running out of time.

00:17:03.609 --> 00:17:05.158
And if it can get through the pipes,

00:17:05.596 --> 00:17:06.602
It can get to anyone,

00:17:06.665 --> 00:17:07.603
Almost anywhere.

00:17:07.697 --> 00:17:09.700
This is gonna happen again soon.

00:17:09.981 --> 00:17:11.483
And we do know one other thing for sure.

00:17:11.515 --> 00:17:13.815
We know this has got something
to do with Bill Carlton.

00:17:13.877 --> 00:17:14.901
It took both his kids.

00:17:14.948 --> 00:17:16.199
And I've been asking around.

00:17:16.324 --> 00:17:17.560
Lucas' dad, Chris

00:17:18.045 --> 00:17:19.328
Bill Carlton's godson.

00:17:20.001 --> 00:17:21.753
Let's go pay Mr. Carlton a visit.

00:17:24.265 --> 00:17:25.532
Mr. Carlton?

00:17:28.254 --> 00:17:30.272
We'd like to ask you a few questions,

00:17:30.351 --> 00:17:31.039
If you don't mind.

00:17:31.102 --> 00:17:33.495
We're from the department I
don't care who you're with.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.614
I've answered enough questions today.

00:17:38.694 --> 00:17:41.432
Your son said he saw
something in that lake.

00:17:42.402 --> 00:17:43.560
What about you?

00:17:44.098 --> 00:17:45.663
You ever see anything out there?

00:17:47.149 --> 00:17:48.119
Mr. Carlton,

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:50.106
Sophie's drowning and Will's death.

00:17:50.403 --> 00:17:51.874
We think there might be a connection,

00:17:51.968 --> 00:17:54.862
To you or your family.
My children are gone.

00:17:58.447 --> 00:17:59.214
It's...

00:18:02.358 --> 00:18:04.032
It's worse than dying.

00:18:11.285 --> 00:18:12.318
Go away...

00:18:13.976 --> 00:18:14.852
Please.

00:18:17.845 --> 00:18:19.081
What do you think?

00:18:20.051 --> 00:18:22.053
I think the poor guy's
been through hell.

00:18:22.836 --> 00:18:24.650
I also think he's not
telling us something.

00:18:24.682 --> 00:18:25.699
So now what?

00:18:28.499 --> 00:18:29.406
What is it?

00:18:33.114 --> 00:18:35.727
Maybe Bill's not the only
one who knows something.

00:18:46.454 --> 00:18:48.237
I'm sorry, but I don't
think it's a good idea.

00:18:48.337 --> 00:18:49.432
I just need to talk to him,

00:18:49.495 --> 00:18:50.559
Just for a few minutes.

00:18:50.731 --> 00:18:52.342
He won't say anything.

00:18:52.827 --> 00:18:54.454
What good's it gonna do? Andrea,

00:18:54.658 --> 00:18:56.269
We think more people might get hurt.

00:18:57.807 --> 00:18:59.215
We think something's
happening out there.

00:18:59.324 --> 00:19:01.953
My husband, the others,
they just drowned.

00:19:02.375 --> 00:19:03.095
That's all.

00:19:03.142 --> 00:19:04.300
If that's what you really believe,

00:19:04.362 --> 00:19:05.129
Then we'll go,

00:19:05.415 --> 00:19:07.386
But if you think there's
even a possibility

00:19:07.699 --> 00:19:09.483
That something else
could be going on here,

00:19:11.079 --> 00:19:12.549
Please let me talk to your son.

00:19:27.968 --> 00:19:29.251
Hey, Lucas.

00:19:30.773 --> 00:19:31.900
You remember me?

00:19:41.156 --> 00:19:42.705
You know, I, uh...

00:19:44.473 --> 00:19:46.773
I wanted to thank you
for that last drawing

00:19:49.928 --> 00:19:51.586
but the thing is

00:19:52.071 --> 00:19:53.448
I need your help again.

00:20:06.418 --> 00:20:08.061
How did you know to draw this?

00:20:11.038 --> 00:20:13.150
Did you know something
bad was gonna happen?

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:16.295
Maybe you could

00:20:16.717 --> 00:20:18.250
Nod yes or no

00:20:18.344 --> 00:20:19.173
For me.

00:20:21.645 --> 00:20:22.693
You're scared.

00:20:27.869 --> 00:20:28.730
It's okay.

00:20:29.559 --> 00:20:30.732
I understand.

00:20:31.249 --> 00:20:32.610
See, when I was your age,

00:20:32.688 --> 00:20:35.176
I saw something real
bad happen to my mom,

00:20:37.934 --> 00:20:39.326
And I was scared, too.

00:20:42.116 --> 00:20:43.524
I didn't feel like talking,

00:20:43.915 --> 00:20:45.057
Just like you,

00:20:46.246 --> 00:20:47.795
But, see, my mom,

00:20:50.204 --> 00:20:52.269
I know she wanted me to be brave.

00:20:55.591 --> 00:20:57.249
I think about that every day.

00:21:02.431 --> 00:21:04.418
And I do my best to be brave.

00:21:08.397 --> 00:21:10.003
And maybe your dad

00:21:12.111 --> 00:21:13.707
Wants you to be brave, too.

00:21:35.668 --> 00:21:36.826
Thanks, Lucas.

00:21:41.696 --> 00:21:44.136
Andrea said the kid never drew
like that till his dad died.

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:47.547
There are cases going
through a traumatic experience

00:21:47.735 --> 00:21:52.386
Could make certain people more sensitive
to premonitions, psychic tendencies.

00:21:52.397 --> 00:21:54.767
What if Lucas is
tapping into it somehow?

00:21:55.059 --> 00:21:57.030
It's only a matter of time
before somebody else drowns,

00:21:57.044 --> 00:21:58.702
So if you got a better lead, please.

00:21:59.458 --> 00:22:00.460
All right.

00:22:00.699 --> 00:22:01.654
We got another house to find.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:05.096
There's about a thousand yellow
two-Stories in this county alone.

00:22:05.722 --> 00:22:06.927
See this church?

00:22:07.381 --> 00:22:09.415
I bet there's less than a
thousand of those around here.

00:22:10.218 --> 00:22:13.002
Oh, college boy thinks he's so smart.

00:22:20.363 --> 00:22:21.709
You know, um...

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.947
What you said about mom.

00:22:27.951 --> 00:22:29.703
You never told me that before.

00:22:30.251 --> 00:22:31.503
It's no big deal.

00:22:35.669 --> 00:22:38.219
Oh, god, we're not gonna have
to hug or anything, are we?

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:06.263
We're sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:23:06.325 --> 00:23:08.735
But does a little boy
live here by chance?

00:23:08.876 --> 00:23:09.877
He might wear

00:23:10.002 --> 00:23:11.082
A blue ball cap,

00:23:11.348 --> 00:23:12.709
Has a red bicycle.

00:23:13.578 --> 00:23:14.626
No, sir.

00:23:16.081 --> 00:23:18.349
Not for a very long time.

00:23:19.898 --> 00:23:22.652
Peter's been gone 35 years now.

00:23:25.591 --> 00:23:27.297
The police never

00:23:28.454 --> 00:23:31.255
I never had any idea what happened.

00:23:34.464 --> 00:23:36.483
He just disappeared.

00:23:37.161 --> 00:23:38.522
Losing him,

00:23:40.697 --> 00:23:41.635
You know,

00:23:43.129 --> 00:23:43.708
It's...

00:23:45.841 --> 00:23:47.702
It's worse than dying.

00:23:52.729 --> 00:23:54.482
Did he disappear from here,

00:23:54.544 --> 00:23:55.530
I mean, from this house?

00:23:55.608 --> 00:23:56.813
He was supposed to

00:23:57.658 --> 00:23:58.784
Ride his bike

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:00.208
Straight home

00:24:00.302 --> 00:24:01.412
After school,

00:24:01.835 --> 00:24:03.352
And he never showed up.

00:24:20.326 --> 00:24:22.250
"Peter Sweeney and Billy Carlton,

00:24:22.521 --> 00:24:23.976
1970."

00:24:29.723 --> 00:24:31.053
You've taken everything,

00:24:33.572 --> 00:24:34.824
Everyone.

00:24:37.785 --> 00:24:39.084
I've got nothing left.

00:24:42.541 --> 00:24:44.012
I didn't understand.

00:24:46.191 --> 00:24:47.490
I didn't believe.

00:24:50.353 --> 00:24:51.698
Now I think I do.

00:24:54.098 --> 00:24:56.147
I think I finally know what you want.

00:25:01.221 --> 00:25:03.427
Okay, this little boy,
Peter Sweeney, vanishes,

00:25:03.474 --> 00:25:05.820
And this is all connected
to Bill Carlton somehow.

00:25:05.852 --> 00:25:07.776
Bill sure as hell seems
to be hiding something.

00:25:07.839 --> 00:25:09.262
And Bill, the people he loves

00:25:09.408 --> 00:25:10.253
They're all getting punished.

00:25:10.457 --> 00:25:11.865
So that Bill did something to Peter.

00:25:12.084 --> 00:25:13.210
What if Bill killed him?

00:25:13.711 --> 00:25:15.056
Peter's spirit would be furious.

00:25:15.135 --> 00:25:16.574
It'd want revenge. It's possible.

00:25:21.988 --> 00:25:23.537
Mr. Carlton!

00:25:26.666 --> 00:25:28.089
Hey. Check it out.

00:25:35.989 --> 00:25:38.148
Mr. Carlton! You need to come back!

00:25:39.353 --> 00:25:41.559
Come out of the water !
Turn the boat around!

00:25:55.364 --> 00:25:56.881
Baby, what's wrong?

00:26:00.011 --> 00:26:01.575
Sam, Dean.

00:26:02.394 --> 00:26:04.287
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:26:05.273 --> 00:26:07.181
So now you're on a first-Name basis.

00:26:08.308 --> 00:26:09.450
What are you doing here?

00:26:09.502 --> 00:26:10.706
I brought you dinner.

00:26:11.051 --> 00:26:13.961
I'm sorry, sweetheart. I
don't really have the time.

00:26:18.081 --> 00:26:19.786
I heard about Bill Carlton.

00:26:20.083 --> 00:26:22.446
Is it true? Is something
going on with the lake?

00:26:24.417 --> 00:26:26.185
Right now, we don't
know what the truth is,

00:26:26.451 --> 00:26:28.939
But I think it might be better
if you and lucas went on home.

00:26:31.874 --> 00:26:33.595
Lucas, hey, what is it?

00:26:33.845 --> 00:26:35.238
Lucas. Lucas.

00:26:35.488 --> 00:26:37.882
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay. Hey,

00:26:37.960 --> 00:26:40.404
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay.

00:27:02.856 --> 00:27:05.985
Okay, just so I'm clear, you see . . .

00:27:06.219 --> 00:27:07.142
Something

00:27:07.627 --> 00:27:09.161
Attack Bill's boat,

00:27:09.630 --> 00:27:10.835
Sending Bill,

00:27:12.238 --> 00:27:14.647
Who is a very good swimmer, by the way,

00:27:14.913 --> 00:27:16.196
Into the drink,

00:27:17.025 --> 00:27:18.746
And you never see him again?

00:27:21.107 --> 00:27:22.640
Yeah, that about sums it up.

00:27:22.687 --> 00:27:24.189
And I'm supposed to believe this,

00:27:24.236 --> 00:27:26.958
Even though I've already
sonar-Swept that entire lake

00:27:27.381 --> 00:27:29.665
And what you're describing is impossible

00:27:30.353 --> 00:27:32.652
And you're not really wildlife service?

00:27:33.939 --> 00:27:34.768
That's right,

00:27:35.018 --> 00:27:35.722
I checked.

00:27:36.004 --> 00:27:37.631
The department's never heard of you two.

00:27:38.137 --> 00:27:38.841
See?

00:27:38.935 --> 00:27:40.843
Now, we can explain that. Enough,

00:27:41.594 --> 00:27:42.674
Please.

00:27:43.816 --> 00:27:46.194
The only reason you're
breathing free air

00:27:46.449 --> 00:27:50.298
Is one of Bill's neighbors saw him
steering out that boat just before you did.

00:27:51.033 --> 00:27:51.691
So

00:27:51.925 --> 00:27:53.505
We have a couple of options here.

00:27:53.803 --> 00:27:55.988
I can arrest you for
impersonating government officials

00:27:56.004 --> 00:27:59.608
And hold you as material witnesses
to Bill Carlton's disappearance,

00:27:59.857 --> 00:28:00.670
Or

00:28:00.983 --> 00:28:03.799
We can chalk this all up to a bad day,

00:28:04.070 --> 00:28:05.525
You get into your car,

00:28:05.665 --> 00:28:08.548
You put this town in
your rearview mirror,

00:28:08.561 --> 00:28:11.704
And you don't ever darken my doorstep

00:28:11.762 --> 00:28:12.476
Again!

00:28:15.182 --> 00:28:16.746
Door number two sounds good.

00:28:16.997 --> 00:28:18.499
That's the one I'd pick.

00:28:33.428 --> 00:28:34.429
Baby...

00:28:36.267 --> 00:28:37.800
What are you doing up?

00:28:40.617 --> 00:28:42.353
Come on, let's go to bed.

00:29:03.668 --> 00:29:04.669
Green.

00:29:04.810 --> 00:29:05.498
What?

00:29:05.623 --> 00:29:07.016
Light's green.

00:29:14.295 --> 00:29:16.126
Ah, the interstate's the other way.

00:29:16.157 --> 00:29:16.767
I know.

00:29:41.056 --> 00:29:43.481
But, Dean, this job, I think it's over.

00:29:43.528 --> 00:29:44.372
I'm not so sure.

00:29:44.419 --> 00:29:47.439
If bill murdered Peter Sweeney
and Peter's spirit got its revenge,

00:29:47.595 --> 00:29:49.692
Case closed. The spirit
should be at rest.

00:29:49.737 --> 00:29:52.053
All right, so what if we take
off and this thing isn't done?

00:29:52.350 --> 00:29:54.374
What if we missed something?
What if more people get hurt?

00:29:54.452 --> 00:29:56.032
But why would you think that?

00:29:57.846 --> 00:29:59.520
Because Lucas was really scared.

00:29:59.786 --> 00:30:01.273
That's what this is about?

00:30:02.243 --> 00:30:04.574
I just don't want to leave
town till I know the kid's okay.

00:30:05.043 --> 00:30:06.029
Who are you,

00:30:06.138 --> 00:30:07.969
And what have you done with my brother?

00:30:10.346 --> 00:30:11.551
Shut up.

00:31:41.888 --> 00:31:43.343
Are you sure about this?

00:31:43.671 --> 00:31:44.970
It's pretty late, man.

00:31:48.291 --> 00:31:49.762
Lucas? Lucas!

00:31:52.703 --> 00:31:53.626
Lucas!

00:32:32.697 --> 00:32:33.761
Can you tell me?

00:32:35.893 --> 00:32:36.754
No

00:32:44.798 --> 00:32:46.503
It doesn't make any sense.

00:32:50.602 --> 00:32:52.135
I'm going crazy.

00:32:53.152 --> 00:32:54.671
No, you're not.

00:32:56.095 --> 00:32:57.269
Tell me what happened.

00:32:57.879 --> 00:32:58.818
Everything.

00:33:03.008 --> 00:33:04.134
I heard...

00:33:07.107 --> 00:33:08.844
I thought I heard...

00:33:11.152 --> 00:33:12.967
There was this voice.

00:33:13.483 --> 00:33:14.453
What did it say?

00:33:14.500 --> 00:33:15.345
It said

00:33:16.305 --> 00:33:18.558
It said, "come play with me."

00:33:26.550 --> 00:33:28.052
What's happening?

00:33:47.342 --> 00:33:49.157
Do you recognize the
kids in these pictures?

00:33:49.282 --> 00:33:50.033
What?

00:33:51.942 --> 00:33:52.834
No, I huh...

00:33:52.912 --> 00:33:56.025
I mean, except that's
my dad right there.

00:33:56.233 --> 00:33:57.594
He must have been about

00:33:58.204 --> 00:33:59.831
12 in these pictures.

00:34:01.460 --> 00:34:02.821
Chris Bar's drowning

00:34:03.102 --> 00:34:05.465
The connection wasn't to Bill
Carlton. It must have been to sheriff.

00:34:05.527 --> 00:34:06.982
Bill and the sheriff,

00:34:07.342 --> 00:34:08.954
They were both involved with Peter.

00:34:09.225 --> 00:34:10.252
What about Chris?

00:34:10.867 --> 00:34:13.026
My dad, what are you talking about?

00:34:13.261 --> 00:34:14.153
Lucas?

00:34:14.873 --> 00:34:16.202
Lucas, what is it?

00:34:22.509 --> 00:34:24.684
Lucas, honey?

00:34:36.441 --> 00:34:38.881
You and Lucas get back to the
house and stay there, okay?

00:35:03.183 --> 00:35:04.435
Peter's bike.

00:35:05.233 --> 00:35:06.281
Who are you?

00:35:09.676 --> 00:35:11.162
Put the gun down, Jake.

00:35:11.866 --> 00:35:13.341
How did you know that was there?

00:35:13.388 --> 00:35:14.233
What happened?

00:35:14.437 --> 00:35:15.985
You and Bill killed Peter,

00:35:16.330 --> 00:35:18.176
Drowned him in the lake,
and then buried the bike?

00:35:19.130 --> 00:35:20.851
You can't bury the truth, Jake.

00:35:22.030 --> 00:35:23.657
Nothing stays buried.

00:35:27.224 --> 00:35:28.726
Go to your room, sweetie.

00:35:30.009 --> 00:35:30.854
Now.

00:35:30.901 --> 00:35:33.172
Lock the door and wait
for me. Don't come out.

00:35:33.546 --> 00:35:34.907
I don't know what the
hell you're talking about.

00:35:34.929 --> 00:35:37.348
You and Bill killed Peter
Sweeney 35 years ago.

00:35:37.442 --> 00:35:38.360
That's what the hell I'm talking about.

00:35:38.365 --> 00:35:38.975
Dad

00:35:39.256 --> 00:35:41.337
And now you got one
seriously pissed-Off spirit.

00:35:41.384 --> 00:35:42.636
It's gonna take Andrea,

00:35:42.745 --> 00:35:43.527
Lucas,

00:35:43.827 --> 00:35:44.812
Everyone you love.

00:35:45.313 --> 00:35:46.393
It's gonna drown them,

00:35:46.799 --> 00:35:48.661
And it's gonna drag their
bodies god knows where.

00:35:48.958 --> 00:35:51.227
So you can feel the Same
pain Peter's mom felt.

00:35:52.088 --> 00:35:53.386
And then after that,

00:35:54.276 --> 00:35:55.325
It's gonna take you,

00:35:55.638 --> 00:35:57.359
And it's not gonna stop until it does.

00:35:58.250 --> 00:35:59.314
How do you know that?

00:35:59.424 --> 00:36:01.880
Because that's exactly
what it did to Bill Carlton.

00:36:01.927 --> 00:36:03.072
Listen to yourselves,

00:36:03.323 --> 00:36:03.933
Both of you.

00:36:03.995 --> 00:36:05.122
You're insane.

00:36:05.169 --> 00:36:07.359
I don't really give a rat's
ass what you think of us,

00:36:08.367 --> 00:36:10.010
But if we're gonna
bring down this spirit,

00:36:10.229 --> 00:36:11.778
We need to find the remains,

00:36:12.044 --> 00:36:12.857
Salt them,

00:36:12.998 --> 00:36:14.125
And burn them into dust.

00:36:14.328 --> 00:36:15.840
Tell me you buried Peter somewhere.

00:36:15.862 --> 00:36:17.593
Tell me you didn't just
let him go in the lake.

00:36:22.960 --> 00:36:25.651
Come play with me.

00:36:29.520 --> 00:36:30.083
Dad,

00:36:30.146 --> 00:36:31.178
Is any of this true?

00:36:31.209 --> 00:36:32.461
No. Don't listen to them.

00:36:32.487 --> 00:36:33.791
They're liars, and they're dangerous.

00:36:33.947 --> 00:36:35.574
Something tried to drown me.

00:36:36.122 --> 00:36:37.405
Chris died on that lake.

00:36:37.436 --> 00:36:38.578
Dad, look at me.

00:36:41.894 --> 00:36:42.566
Tell me you

00:36:42.629 --> 00:36:44.162
You didn't kill anyone.

00:36:54.050 --> 00:36:55.161
Oh, my god.

00:36:59.213 --> 00:37:00.709
Billy and I were at the lake.

00:37:03.791 --> 00:37:06.420
Peter was the smallest
one. We always bullied him,

00:37:06.952 --> 00:37:08.062
But this time...

00:37:09.319 --> 00:37:10.414
It got rough.

00:37:15.343 --> 00:37:16.985
We were holding his
head under the water.

00:37:17.882 --> 00:37:19.134
We didn't mean to,

00:37:19.963 --> 00:37:21.653
But we held him under too long,

00:37:21.778 --> 00:37:22.983
And he drowned.

00:37:29.975 --> 00:37:31.289
We let the body go,

00:37:32.009 --> 00:37:33.073
And it sank.

00:37:40.146 --> 00:37:41.382
Oh, Andrea.

00:37:44.485 --> 00:37:45.659
We were kids.

00:37:46.159 --> 00:37:47.051
We were so scared.

00:37:47.082 --> 00:37:48.099
It was a mistake,

00:37:48.115 --> 00:37:48.970
But, Andrea,

00:37:49.262 --> 00:37:51.671
To say that I have anything
to do with these drownings,

00:37:51.702 --> 00:37:52.829
With Chris,

00:37:53.251 --> 00:37:54.894
Because of some ghost

00:37:55.176 --> 00:37:56.725
It's not rational.

00:37:57.746 --> 00:37:59.013
All right, listen to me,

00:37:59.514 --> 00:38:00.468
All of you.

00:38:01.141 --> 00:38:02.643
We need to get you away from this lake

00:38:02.737 --> 00:38:04.379
As far as we can right now.

00:38:08.304 --> 00:38:08.882
Lucas!

00:38:12.705 --> 00:38:14.754
Come play with me.

00:38:15.662 --> 00:38:16.444
Lucas!

00:38:16.636 --> 00:38:19.327
Lucas! Stay where you are!

00:38:38.315 --> 00:38:39.410
Oh, my god!

00:38:42.883 --> 00:38:44.072
Andrea, stay there.

00:38:44.213 --> 00:38:45.293
No, Lucas!

00:38:45.345 --> 00:38:46.643
We'll get him. Stay on the dock.

00:38:52.929 --> 00:38:53.904
Lucas?

00:38:56.622 --> 00:38:57.420
Sam?

00:38:59.313 --> 00:39:00.862
Lucas, where are you?

00:39:05.138 --> 00:39:05.764
Peter,

00:39:05.936 --> 00:39:06.906
If you can hear me,

00:39:08.068 --> 00:39:09.006
Please, Peter,

00:39:09.038 --> 00:39:09.789
I'm sorry.

00:39:11.275 --> 00:39:12.104
I'm so... Dad, no!

00:39:12.151 --> 00:39:13.215
I'm so sorry.

00:39:13.716 --> 00:39:14.279
Peter.

00:39:14.514 --> 00:39:15.202
Lucas

00:39:15.499 --> 00:39:17.658
He's j... he's just a little boy.

00:39:18.367 --> 00:39:20.448
Please, it's not his fault. It's mine.

00:39:20.589 --> 00:39:21.762
Please take me!

00:39:22.763 --> 00:39:23.311
Jake,

00:39:23.373 --> 00:39:23.733
No!

00:39:25.032 --> 00:39:26.487
Listen, let it be over!

00:39:28.748 --> 00:39:29.436
Dad

00:39:30.268 --> 00:39:31.099
Daddy!

00:39:33.632 --> 00:39:34.492
No

00:39:44.486 --> 00:39:45.346
No...

00:40:25.737 --> 00:40:26.473
Look,

00:40:27.302 --> 00:40:28.679
We're not gonna save everybody.

00:40:31.312 --> 00:40:31.969
I know.

00:40:32.751 --> 00:40:33.502
Sam,

00:40:33.878 --> 00:40:34.566
Dean.

00:40:34.707 --> 00:40:35.473
Hey.

00:40:37.194 --> 00:40:38.352
We're glad we caught you.

00:40:38.790 --> 00:40:39.682
We just, um,

00:40:40.875 --> 00:40:42.377
We made you lunch for the road.

00:40:43.159 --> 00:40:45.897
Lucas insisted on making
the sandwiches himself.

00:40:47.372 --> 00:40:48.421
Can I give it to them now?

00:40:50.345 --> 00:40:50.955
Of course.

00:40:52.174 --> 00:40:53.989
Come on, Lucas, let's
load this in the car.

00:41:00.611 --> 00:41:01.549
How you holding up?

00:41:03.990 --> 00:41:06.916
It's just gonna take a long time to
sort through everything, you know?

00:41:10.863 --> 00:41:12.459
Andrea, I'm sorry.

00:41:14.054 --> 00:41:15.259
You saved my son.

00:41:17.043 --> 00:41:18.779
I can't ask for more than that.

00:41:22.454 --> 00:41:23.315
Dad loved me.

00:41:24.441 --> 00:41:25.693
He loved Lucas.

00:41:26.679 --> 00:41:27.680
No matter what he did,

00:41:27.701 --> 00:41:28.822
I just have to...

00:41:30.579 --> 00:41:31.628
Hold on to that.

00:41:37.825 --> 00:41:38.643
All right,

00:41:38.806 --> 00:41:40.277
If you're gonna be talking now,

00:41:40.572 --> 00:41:43.580
This is a very important phrase, so
I want you to repeat it one more time.

00:41:43.776 --> 00:41:44.730
Zeppelin rules!

00:41:44.734 --> 00:41:46.140
That's right. Up high.

00:41:49.826 --> 00:41:51.786
Take care of your mom, okay?

00:41:59.731 --> 00:42:01.268
Thank you.

00:42:06.444 --> 00:42:07.719
Sam, move your ass.

00:42:08.112 --> 00:42:10.172
We're gonna run out of
daylight before we hit the road.



